# GATED — this stack is intentionally not deployed yet.
#
# getStackFiles (components/DockgeLxc.ts) skips any stack directory containing a
# `.ignore`, so while this file exists the compose below is inert: nothing is
# rendered, nothing is copied to the host, and no reference in .env is resolved.
# That last point is the reason this file exists rather than the stack simply
# being merged live — see the "unlock" checklist.
#
# This is piece G' of docs/cluster-consolidation/07-authentik-to-alpha-site.md
# (vault#84 decision D4): the estate's SSO moves off Kubernetes onto alpha-site.
# Deleting this file is NOT the cutover. It only makes the stack deployable
# against an empty database while SGC keeps serving every hostname. The cutover
# itself is section 4 of that document, steps 3 onward.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UNLOCK CHECKLIST — every item must be true before deleting this file
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. fsync/flush test on alpha-site's USB SSD is recorded and passing (section
#    3.1). This is the one genuinely unmeasured risk in the whole piece, and it
#    is specifically a database risk: everything already on that Pi survives a
#    bridge that ignores FUA, and Postgres does not.
#
# 2. Create the OpenBao secret this stack's postgres password comes from. It
#    does NOT exist yet — it is the only new secret the stack needs; the other
#    three (authentik-secret-key, authentik-token, authentik-admin) are already
#    live and used by SGC today.
#
#      bao kv put secrets/clusters/alpha-site/apps/authentik/postgres password=<generated>
#
#    A missing item is not a soft failure: the resolver hands whole files to
#    vals, and an unresolvable reference aborts the ENTIRE stacks/home program,
#    not just this stack (HO#636). That is what this gate is protecting.
#
# 3. Declare the database in the shared Postgres instance by adding this line
#    to docker/alpha-site/postgres/.env-local, using the SAME field as .env
#    here so the two can never drift:
#
#      PGAPP_AUTHENTIK_PASSWORD="ref+openbao<colon>//secrets/clusters/alpha-site/apps/authentik/postgres#/password"
#
#    Replace <colon> with a literal colon. It is written this way ON PURPOSE:
#    the resolver is a plain regex with no notion of comments, vals expands
#    references wherever they appear — comments included — and a reference-shaped
#    string in a comment fails exactly like a real one. Never write a resolvable
#    scheme in a comment in this tree, not even a disabled one.
#
#    That one line is all the backup wiring needed: stacks/backups already
#    rclone-pulls /opt/stacks-data/ for every Dockge host, so the pg_dump ->
#    backrest -> PBS chain covers this database generically the moment the role
#    exists (section 2.1). Proving the RESTORE half is still manual (3.2).
#
# 4. Re-measure the Pi's headroom (`node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes`,
#    cluster="alpha-site"). The ~1.5-2 GiB figure in section 2.2 is arithmetic
#    against a 2026-07-30 measurement taken before bao-transit and bao-standby
#    landed on this host.
#
# 5. Break-glass paths fixed (section 3.3) and piece 03 landed (section 3.4).
#
# After deleting this file, `pulumi up` on stacks/home deploys authentik here
# against a FRESH, EMPTY database. Confirm it starts healthy against that empty
# DB before restoring anything into it.
